# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Test / coverage artifacts
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.json
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
*-junit.xml
# CI-shard artifacts: the per-shard log is covered by *.log below, these
# two are written straight into backend/ by the shard step, so a developer
# reproducing a CI run locally would otherwise find them untracked.
pytest-stack-dump*.txt
pytest-deadline-*.flag

# Node
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/

# Node test artifacts
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Local secrets — never commit. The non-secret test template
# (backend/.env.ci) and the documented example (backend/.env.example)
# are deliberately tracked.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.ci
!.env.example

# Runtime state
#
# 2026-09-28: the whole state family moved into `.pdt/` — state.db and its
# WAL siblings, the boot counter and the rotating snapshot dir. The
# individual entries below are kept on purpose rather than replaced: if
# something ever writes a state file back to the repository root, it stays
# ignored instead of becoming committable. That is the safe direction for
# this one to fail in.
.pdt/
state.db
state.db-*
# Runtime artifacts that live beside state.db. ``backups/state-db/`` is the
# rotating state-db snapshot dir; ``pdt_server_boot_id`` is a boot counter the
# server bumps on every start. Both are per-machine, recreated on demand, and
# must never ship — in the first export they were untracked-but-*not*-ignored,
# so a plain `git add -A` would have committed seven .db snapshots and the
# counter into the public repo.
backups/
pdt_server_boot_id
# The pre-rename name. Still on disk from an earlier run; ignoring it
# keeps a stray `git add -A` from recommitting it.
ac_server_boot_id
*.log
logs/
bridge.out

# A plan artefact written into the wrong place.
#
# The canonical home for a plan's ``verification_plan.json`` is
# ``plans/<id>/``, which every reader in the backend resolves via its own
# ``plan_dir``. One was committed at ``backend/verification_plan.json``
# instead — nothing reads that path, so it shipped a stale plan's
# verification points into the repository and stayed there. Pin the
# pattern so a run that resolves ``plan_dir`` wrongly cannot re-add it.
backend/verification_plan.json
backend/verification_report.json

# Plan artifacts are runtime data, not source.
#
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose: an unanchored ``plans/`` also
# matches ``backend/tests/fixtures/plans/``, which silently un-tracked a
# fixture that ``test_server_json_cleanup.py`` reads at runtime — the
# test passes on a machine that has the directory and fails on a fresh
# clone, which is the worst possible shape for a fixture.
/plans/

# Nightly CI writes its result envelope here. It is produced by the
# operator's local nightly runner, so it belongs to that machine, not to
# the repo. Since 2026-09-28 it lives at ``.pdt/nightly-results.json``
# and is covered by the ``.pdt/`` rule above; this entry is the pre-move
# name, kept for the same reason as the state-file entries — a stray
# write back to the repository root should stay ignored.
.pdt-nightly-results.json

# MkDocs build output (docs site). Generated by `mkdocs build`; the
# source is docs/ and the config is mkdocs.yml, so the rendered tree is
# an artifact, not content.
site/

# Local configuration — operator-owned, never committed.
#
# Everything deployment-specific lives here: which providers you have and
# which tier each belongs to, and the provider-order contract written by
# whichever producer you run. Templates ship in ``example/``; copy one in
# and rename it to activate it. See README.md. Committing a real config
# would publish one operator's provider set as if it were everyone's.
.config/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# E2E onboarding + frontend screenshots dropped by the operator's
# manual DOM walk. The pytest layer cannot drive a browser (the
# project pins no playwright / selenium, and ``mcp__puppeteer__*``
# only lives in agent sessions), so the contract is "the operator
# produces ``backend/tests/e2e/_artifacts/onboarding_<step>.png``
# as evidence; pytest never writes there". A screenshot committed
# by accident would still surface the developer's machine in the
# public repo, so the pattern is anchored under ``backend/tests/``
# rather than left at the repo root.
backend/tests/e2e/_artifacts/

# Project instructions for the operator running this checkout.
#
# Kept local on purpose: it carries the operator-policy sections (how to
# run the fleet, which subsystems live where) that are about one
# installation, not about the product. The published repo documents the
# product; this file documents my machine.
CLAUDE.md
